    "category": "Reduction of Risk Potential",
    "type": "single",
    "number": 10,
    "prompt": "The LPN is caring for a woman who delivered a healthy 7-lb baby boy 24 hours ago. Baseline vital signs were blood pressure (BP) = 90/64, temperature (T) = 97.6°F, pulse (P) = 72, and respirations (R) = 14. Which ﬁ nding is of greatest concern? Editorial review has deemed that any suppressed content does not materially affect the overall learning experience. Cengage Learning reserves the right to remove additional content at any time if subsequent rights restrictions require it.",
