    "rationale": "Lithium is excreted from the body as a sodium salt. A low-salt diet is likely to cause the lithium levels to rise and cause lithium toxicity. The normal serum lithium level is 0.5 to 1.4 mEq/L, so a level of 1.0 mEq/ mL is within normal limits. Weight is a common but not dangerous side effect of lithium. The drug should be taken with plenty of water and after meals to minimize GI side effects."
