    "rationale": "Most cases of restlessness in combination with lethargy are due to hypoxia. Hypoxia will cause an irregular pulse and rapid shallow respirations. The client may be in pain. However, the priority is to treat anoxia ﬁ first and then reassess the client before giving analgesia. The nurse will inspect the wounds for drainage on a regular basis. The data do not suggest an immediate need to inspect the wound or irrigate the nasogastric tube. The data are more consistent with hypoxia than pain. Airway takes precedence over pain."
