    "rationale": "Hypomagnesemia is characterized by low serum calcium and potassium levels. The nurse would suspect low serum potassium levels because the client is taking furosemide (Lasix), a potassium-depleting diuretic. The nurse would suspect hypocalcemia because the client has hyperreﬂ exia as evidenced by muscle cramps, facial tics, and positive Chvostek’s and Trousseau’s signs. Altered acid-base balance does not usually occur with hypomagnesemia. ECG changes are not typically associated with hypomagnesemia."
